				<div class="entry-content woocommerce-Tabs-panel woocommerce-Tabs-panel--description wd-active panel wc-tab" id="tab-description" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-title-description" data-accordion-index="description" style="display: block;">
					<div class="wc-tab-inner wd-entry-content">
													

<h2><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter Overview</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> is built for solar systems that need more than daytime PV generation. It combines </span><b>solar power, battery storage and grid supply</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> in one system while providing a dedicated backup output for loads that need power during grid interruptions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With a </span><b>4000W nominal AC output</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, this inverter fits single-phase residential and selected small commercial applications. Its </span><b>24V battery architecture</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> is suitable for buyers who specifically need a low-voltage battery system. The inverter supports </span><b>lead-acid and lithium-ion batteries</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, with a battery voltage range of </span><b>20V to 30V</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">On the solar side, the inverter accepts up to </span><b>6000W of PV input</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and provides an </span><b>85V–450V MPPT operating range</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. The maximum MPPT charging current reaches </span><b>120A</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, giving the system strong battery-charging capability when adequate solar generation is available.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter also supports </span><b>diesel generator integration</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, </span><b>smart load support</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, Wi-Fi/RS485/RS232 communication and IP54 protection.</span></p>
<h2><b>Why This Hybrid Inverter Stands Out</b></h2>
<h3><b>6000W PV Input for a 4kW Inverter</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">One of the key advantages of the </span><b>itel 4kw hybrid inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> is its </span><b>6000W maximum PV input power</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> against a 4000W rated AC output. This allows a properly designed system to install a larger solar array than the inverter’s AC rating, subject to the specified PV voltage, current and installation limits.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For buyers searching for </span><b>itel 4kw pv</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, the important point is that this model accepts up to </span><b>6000W PV input</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, with a maximum PV voltage of </span><b>500V</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and an MPPT voltage range of </span><b>85V–450V</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<h3><b>120A Maximum MPPT Charging Current</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter supports up to </span><b>120A MPPT charging current</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. This helps make better use of available solar generation for charging a connected 24V battery bank.</span></p>
<h3><b>Dual Output for Main and Smart Loads</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>4KW Pro</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> supports </span><b>smart load and main load</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> outputs. This gives installers more flexibility when separating priority loads from other electrical loads in a hybrid solar installation.</span></p>
<h3><b>Fast Backup Switching</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The backup system provides a </span><b>10ms UPS switching time</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and </span><b>20ms switching time for appliances</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. This makes the backup output suitable for selected essential loads where a fast transfer between power sources is important.</span></p>
<h3><b>IP54 Protection</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter has an </span><b>IP54 ingress protection rating</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. For users searching </span><b>itel 4kw ip54</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, this means the inverter has protection against limited dust ingress and water splashes from specified directions. Proper installation, ventilation and protection from direct environmental exposure are still important.</span></p>
<h2><b>Best For</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> is a suitable option for:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Homes needing battery backup</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> during power interruptions.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Users looking for an </span><b>itel 4kw inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> for a single-phase solar system.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Buyers planning a </span><b>24V low-voltage battery system</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Solar systems requiring up to </span><b>6000W PV input</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Users who want both </span><b>solar charging and grid/generator charging</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Installations where selected loads need a dedicated backup output.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Buyers who want </span><b>smart load support</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> in their hybrid solar system.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Areas where load shedding makes battery-backed solar useful.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2><b>Not Ideal For</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This model is not the right choice for every solar installation. Its </span><b>4000W rated AC output</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> makes it unsuitable for systems that require a higher continuous inverter output. It also uses a </span><b>24V battery architecture</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, so it should not be selected for a system specifically designed around a higher-voltage battery bank.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It is also not an appropriate choice for a three-phase electrical requirement because this is a </span><b>single-phase inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<h2><b>Solar PV Input and MPPT Performance</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> supports a maximum PV input power of </span><b>6000W</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. Its maximum PV input voltage is </span><b>500V</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, while the MPPT operating voltage range is </span><b>85V–450V</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The PV input specifications are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum PV Input Power:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 6000W</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum PV Input Voltage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 500V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Start-Up Voltage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 80V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>MPPT Voltage Range:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 85V–450V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum PV Input Current:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 13A</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>MPPT Trackers:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 1</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For anyone searching </span><b>itel 4kw pv</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, these limits are important when designing the solar array. Panel string design should keep the expected </span><b>Voc and Isc</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, temperature effects and MPPT operating limits within the inverter’s permitted range.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4kw pro inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> therefore needs to be paired with a properly designed PV array rather than simply connecting panels based on total wattage alone.</span></p>
<h2><b>Battery Compatibility and Energy Storage</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter uses a </span><b>24V low-voltage battery architecture</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and supports </span><b>lead-acid, lithium-ion and user-defined battery settings</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its battery specifications include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Battery Type:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> Lead-acid / Lithium-ion / User Defined</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Rated Battery Voltage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 24V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Battery Voltage Range:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 20V–30V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum MPPT Charging Current:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 120A</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum Mains/Generator Charging Current:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 10A</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum Discharging Current:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 160A</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter is therefore suitable for buyers specifically looking for a </span><b>24V hybrid solar inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> with lithium-ion battery capability.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For lithium battery installations, the battery’s voltage, BMS communication requirements and compatibility should be confirmed before installation. The available communication interfaces include </span><b>Wi-Fi, RS485 and RS232</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, along with a dry-contact interface.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">If you are searching </span><b>itel lithium battery 4kw price in pakistan</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, it is important to understand that </span><b>4kW refers to the inverter’s rated AC output, not the battery’s capacity</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. Battery capacity and battery price depend on the battery model, voltage, Ah rating and energy capacity. The inverter itself supports lithium-ion batteries but does not have a battery capacity of 4kW.</span></p>
<h2><b>Backup Power and Load-Shedding Performance</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For Pakistani homes dealing with load shedding, the </span><b>backup output</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> is one of the most important features of a hybrid inverter.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> provides a </span><b>4000W nominal AC output</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and supports fast transfer to backup operation. Its switching specification is </span><b>10ms for UPS mode</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> and </span><b>20ms for appliances</b><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter also provides surge capability of </span><b>8000W for 5 seconds</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. Its overload capability is specified at different durations, allowing short-duration higher loads within the stated limits.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Backup performance depends on the connected battery, battery condition, available solar power and the actual load. High-starting-current appliances should be assessed carefully before connecting them to the backup output.</span></p>
<h2><b>Generator and Smart Load Support</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The inverter supports </span><b>diesel generator operation</b><span style="font-weight: 400">, giving users another charging and power-source option when solar generation and grid availability are insufficient.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It also supports </span><b>smart load control</b><span style="font-weight: 400">. This can be useful when certain loads need to be managed separately from priority household loads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For a hybrid system, generator integration should be planned according to the inverter’s electrical limits and the generator’s output characteristics.</span></p>
<h2><b>Monitoring and Communication</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The </span><b>itel 4KW Pro Hybrid Inverter</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> provides several communication interfaces for system monitoring and control.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Supported interfaces include:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Wi-Fi</b></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>RS485</b></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>RS232</b></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Dry Contact</b></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These interfaces can support system communication, monitoring and control functions depending on the connected equipment and installation configuration.</span></p>
<h2><b>Technical Specifications</b></h2>
<h3><b>Solar PV Input</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum PV Input Power:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 6000W</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum PV Input Voltage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 500V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Start-Up Voltage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 80V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>MPPT Voltage Range:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 85V–450V</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Maximum Input Current:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 13A</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>MPPT Trackers:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> 1</span></li>
</ul>
<h3><b>Battery</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><b>Battery Type:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> Lead-acid / Lithium-ion / User Defined</span></li>
